  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::93107",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Kcnc3, Kcna7, and Kcnv2, all of which are involved in the same biological process—Delayed Rectifier Potassium Channel Activity. This activity is ultimately linked to the participation of Kcng4, suggesting a potential mechanistic pathway where Guanidine may influence Kcng4 through modulation of potassium channel function. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust and reliable association, supported by multiple independent interactions. The shared involvement of these potassium channels in the same pathway implies that Guanidine may exert its effects through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating channel activity or function. The evidence suggests that Guanidine could potentially affect Kcng4 via a pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and functional role of this interaction.",
